  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "One of the Oregon Ghost series, this cultivar is similar in leaf shape and size to its parent, the well-known 'Beni shigitatsu sawa', but with a network of green veins on a paler whitish green background. It is especially noteworthy in the spring and early summer when the young leaves are pink-flushed from the outer margins. It is estimated to form a broad shrubby tree up to 10 ft. (3 m) tall and needs some protection from the afternoon sun."
  },
